---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const defaultFunction = `f <- function(x, y) {
  y / (2*x + 1)
}`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Runge-Kutta and IVP Methods — CMNA" description="Compare Euler, midpoint, and fourth-order Runge-Kutta on arbitrary R differential equations.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Differential equations · CMNA Laboratory</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Turn a derivative into a trajectory.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Euler trusts one slope. Midpoint samples again halfway through the step.
        Fourth-order Runge-Kutta asks four questions before deciding where to land.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-column">
      <article class="content">
        <h2>One differential equation, three stepping rules</h2>
        <p>
          Give the laboratory any R function <code>f(x,y)</code> describing
          (y' = f(x,y)). The three CMNA methods start from the same initial
          condition and step size, so their different trajectories come entirely
          from how much slope information each method uses.
        </p>
      </article>
      <aside class="callout">
        <strong>RK4's four slopes</strong>
        <p>
          The playable view marks the four stage evaluations inside each RK4 step.
          The final update uses weights (1/6, 1/3, 1/3, 1/6).
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section lab-section">
    <div class="shell" data-ivp-lab>
      <div class="lab-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Bring your own ODE</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Write the derivative in R.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Then watch three numerical methods advance the same initial value problem.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lab-expression"><span>Runtime</span><code data-status>Preparing R…</code></div>
      </div>

      <div class="r-guided-grid">
        <section class="r-guided-editor">
          <div class="r-editor-label"><span>R</span><small>Define <code>f(x,y)</code></small></div>
          <textarea class="r-editor r-function-editor" data-r-function spellcheck="false">{defaultFunction}</textarea>
          <div class="r-guided-controls">
            <label>x₀<input type="number" value="0" step="any" data-x0 /></label>
            <label>y₀<input type="number" value="1" step="any" data-y0 /></label>
            <label>step h<input type="number" value="0.05" step="any" data-h /></label>
            <label>steps n<input type="number" value="40" min="1" max="200" step="1" data-n /></label>
          </div>
          <div class="r-run-row">
            <button class="button r-run" type="button" data-run disabled>Advance in R</button>
            <button class="r-reset" type="button" data-reset>Reset R session</button>
          </div>
        </section>
        <aside class="r-guided-primer">
          <h3>Change h before changing anything else.</h3>
          <p>
            A smaller step gives every method more opportunities to correct its
            course. Try doubling and halving <code>h</code> while keeping the total
            span roughly comparable.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="lab-summary" data-summary></div>
      <div class="comparison-legend">
        <span><i style="background:#8b949c"></i>Euler</span>
        <span><i class="legend-gold"></i>Midpoint</span>
        <span><i class="legend-azure"></i>RK4</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-plot-frame"><svg class="lab-plot" role="img" aria-label="Euler, midpoint, and RK4 solution paths" data-plot></svg></div>
      <div class="lab-stepper">
        <button class="button secondary-on-light" type="button" data-play disabled>Play steps</button>
        <label><span data-step-label>RK4 step</span><input type="range" min="0" max="1" value="0" data-step disabled /></label>
      </div>
      <p class="lab-status" data-step-detail></p>
      <div class="lab-table-wrap">
        <table class="lab-table">
          <thead><tr><th>step</th><th>x</th><th>y</th><th>s₁</th><th>s₂</th><th>s₃</th><th>s₄</th><th>next y</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody data-rows></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script is:inline type="module" src="/js/ivp-lab.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
